# Firebase config for the Fable build
#
# app/google-services.json in git is a CI stub (project_id = mekasa-ci-stub).
# FirebaseGate skips FirebaseApp initialisation for that project id, so the
# app builds and runs (offline preview + debug test-token sign-in) without
# real credentials.
#
# For email / Google sign-in against the real project:
#   1. Firebase Console -> Project settings -> Your apps -> Add Android app for
#        com.fernandogator.mekasa.fable
#        com.fernandogator.mekasa.fable.debug
#      (add the debug SHA-1 for Google sign-in).
#   2. Download google-services.json and save it as app/google-services.real.json
#      (gitignored), then copy it over app/google-services.json locally.
#   3. Make sure an OAuth "Web client" (client_type 3) exists so the
#      google-services plugin generates R.string.default_web_client_id.
#   4. Enable Email/Password and Google providers in Authentication.
